  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "The implementation is complete and consistent. Summary of changes:\n\n**`src/state.mjs`** (the shared parser state machine):\n- **CRLF across chunks**: a CR now sets `pendingCR` and is resolved by the *next* character, so `\\r` at a chunk boundary followed by `\\n` in the next chunk correctly ends one record. A CR not followed by LF (including at EOF) throws `BARE_CR`.\n- **Doubled quotes across chunks**: `afterQuote` + `\"` now appends a literal `\"` and returns to `quoted` mode, so `\"\"` split across chunks unescapes correctly. Previously this threw `INVALID_QUOTE`.\n- **Closing-quote handling**: `afterQuote` accepts `,`, LF, or CRLF (via `pendingCR`); any other character throws `INVALID_QUOTE`. A CR after a closing quote is treated as a line-ending candidate, so a bare CR there yields `BARE_CR` per the CR rule.\n- Added an `endRecord` helper that finishes the field, finishes the record, and resets mode/CR state, keeping record termination uniform.\n\n**`src/line.mjs`**: simplified `consumeLine` to only end a record on LF (CR is handled by the buffered `pendingCR` path), with a comment documenting the CRLF requirement. It is no longer on the hot path but stays consistent.\n\n**Unchanged**: `parseRows`, `readItems`, `countItems` exports and signatures; `tokenizer.mjs` (already validates array/string types and handles empty chunks); `item-schema.mjs` (`COLUMN_COUNT`/`EMPTY_ID`); `escape.mjs`; and the independent `slug`/`checksum` helpers. Both consumers already route through the single `parseRows`, so they see identical records and errors.\n\n**What was checked**: I traced the grammar by hand against the new state machine — CRLF split across chunks, doubled quotes split across chunks, quoted commas/line breaks, bare CR at EOF, `INVALID_QUOTE` after a closing quote, empty input → `[]`, blank line → `['']`, and no extra trailing record after a final line ending. No tests were executed (no shell/test runner available), so I am not claiming the test suite passed.",
